  "notes": "INTENSITY:\n{引|ひ}っ{張|ぱ}る is more emphatic and forceful than {引|ひ}く. The っ{張|ぱ}る pattern adds intensity.\n\nCOMPOUND VERB FORMATION:\n{引|ひ}く + っ + {張|は}る = emphatic pulling action\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {足|あし}を{引|ひ}っ{張|ぱ}る: to hold someone back, to be a burden\n- {引|ひ}っ{張|ぱ}りだこ: very much in demand (lit. \"pulled octopus\")\n- チームを{引|ひ}っ{張|ぱ}る: to lead a team\n\nRELATED COMPOUNDS:\n- {引|ひ}っ{張|ぱ}り{込|こ}む: to drag into\n- {引|ひ}っ{張|ぱ}り{出|だ}す: to pull out, to drag out",
